<!-- Managed by ai-repo-template's install-user. Edits between these markers are replaced on the next install. -->
- Open pull requests, never merge them. A human merges. Don't enable auto-merge either.
- Read `~/.claude/PROFILE.md` if it exists: it says how I like to work.
- Before a non-trivial change, propose the approach and the files you'll touch.
- Before calling work done, run the repo's checks and say what passed.
- In repos set up from ai-repo-template, config lives in `.claude/` and is committed. The plan, product brief and decisions live in the notes: `~/claude-notes/<repo>/`, outside the repo and never committed, or `claude-notes/` inside it. `.claude/CLAUDE.md` names which.
<!-- ai-repo-template:end -->
